### **Results**
This study aimed to assess treatment adherence and health status among HIV-positive clients at Faith Alive Foundation, Jos, Nigeria, and to examine the relationship between them. A total of 609 patients were included in the analysis. The health status was primarily measured through virological outcomes (specifically baseline and current viral load suppression, defined as <1000 copies/ml and ≥1000 copies/ml). Other health status measures included HIV staging/progress, weight stability, presence of opportunistic infection, presence of symptoms of sexually transmitted diseases and other co-mobidities. The findings are presented below.


#### Socio-demographic characteristics of respondents
```{r}

adherence %>% 
  select(Gender = gender,
         `Age (years)` = age_years,
         `Age group (years)` = age_group,
         Religion = religion,
         `Marital status` = marital_status,
         `Education level` = level_of_education,
         `Employment status`= employment_status,
         `Residence in Plateau state` = do_you_live_in_plateau_state,
         `Sexually active` = are_you_sexually_active,
         `More than one sexual partner` = if_yes_do_you_have_more_than_one_sexual_partner
         ) %>% 
  tbl_summary(
    statistic = list(
      all_continuous() ~  c("{min}, {max}",
                            "{mean} ({sd})",
                            "{median} ({p25}, {p75})"
                            
      ),
      all_categorical() ~ "{n} ({p}%)"),
    digits = list(all_continuous() ~ 1,
                  all_categorical() ~ c(0, 1)),
    type = list(all_continuous()    ~ "continuous2",
                where(is.logical)   ~ "categorical",
                where(is.character) ~ "categorical",
                all_dichotomous()   ~ "categorical"),
    percent = "column",
    missing_text = "Missing"
  ) %>%
  modify_header(label ~ "**Variable**") %>%
  bold_labels()



```
  
    
    A total of 609 participants were included in this study. The cohort was predominantly female (449, 73.7%), with a smaller proportion of male participants (160, 26.3%).

Age: The age of participants ranged from 18 to 87 years. The mean (SD) age was 44.7 (12.0) years, with a median (IQR) age of 44.0 (36.0, 51.0) years, indicating a roughly symmetric distribution around middle adulthood. When categorized, the largest age group was 35-49 years (286, 47.0%), followed by 50-64 years (171, 28.1%) and 18-34 years (120, 19.7%). A small proportion of participants were aged 65 years or older (32, 5.3%).

Religion: The majority of participants identified as Christian (523, 85.9%), with 86 (14.1%) identifying as Muslim. Regarding marital status, most participants were married (394, 64.7%), while 115 (18.9%) were single, 65 (10.7%) were widowed, and 35 (5.7%) were separated.

Education: Educational attainment was varied: the highest proportion of participants had a secondary level education (350, 57.5%), followed by tertiary education (117, 19.2%). A combined 23.3% of participants had either no formal education (72, 11.8%) or only a primary level education (70, 11.5%). 

Employment status: The vast majority of participants were engaged in some form of work, with self-employment being the most common (362, 59.4%), followed by those who were employed (147, 24.1%). A minority were unemployed (92, 15.1%) or retired (8, 1.3%).

Residence and Sexual activity: Most participants reported residing in Plateau state (450, 73.9%). The majority of the cohort also reported being sexually active (444, 72.9%). Among those who were sexually active, a large majority (369, 83.1%) reported having only one sexual partner (interpreted here as being in a mutually monogamous relationship), while 75 (16.9%) reported having more than one sexual partner.


